<div class="help-facility-note"><span class="help-note-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span><div><strong>AICS/SWAD data and access are separate from MAIFIP.</strong><span>AICS assistance records and the centralized Region II fund are managed in the AICS workspace. SWAD office membership controls office-specific access. The shared interface does not merge AICS records, accounts, funds, or messages with MAIFIP.</span></div></div>
<div class="help-sections">
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">ACCOUNT & ACCESS</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="3"/><path d="M5 20v-1a7 7 0 0 1 14 0v1"/></g></svg>Login, Accounts & Permissions</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details open><summary>How do I sign in?</summary><p>Use the credentials assigned to your account. If you cannot sign in, confirm that your account is active and that you are using the correct workspace. Do not share your password or authentication codes.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who manages user types and office assignments?</summary><p>The authorized LPGMA System Administrator manages AICS account access and office assignments. Your available pages and actions depend on your assigned role and office. Similar-looking controls do not grant additional permissions.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can an AICS account access MAIFIP records?</summary><p>No. AICS and MAIFIP use separate program data and authorization rules. A user must be explicitly authorized in the relevant workspace; visual similarities do not permit cross-system record access.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should I do if my account or office assignment is incorrect?</summary><p>Submit a support ticket with your username, the expected office, the page you were trying to access, and the error shown. Never include your password.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">ASSISTANCE RECORDS</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="5" y="4" width="14" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M8 8h8M8 12h8M8 16h5"/></g></svg>New Assistance, Masterlist & Status</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details><summary>How do I encode a new assistance record?</summary><p>Open <strong>New Assistance</strong>, complete the required client and beneficiary details, select the appropriate SWAD Office and assistance type, enter the required contact number, and complete the Province → Municipality/City → Barangay fields. Review the details before saving.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the Control No. format?</summary><p>New AICS assistance entries use the configured year-based control number format. Check the generated control number after saving and include it when requesting help about a record.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I find a record?</summary><p>Open the Masterlist, use the search field and available filters, and check the Control No., beneficiary, office, status, and submission date. Use the sheet view when you need a spreadsheet-style view of the permitted records.</p></details>
<details><summary>What do WAITING, RELEASED, and CANCELLED mean?</summary><p><strong>WAITING</strong> means the entry is still being processed. <strong>RELEASED</strong> means assistance has been released. <strong>CANCELLED</strong> means the entry has been cancelled. Only users with the appropriate permission may update a status.</p></details>
<details><summary>What happens when a WAITING entry expires?</summary><p>The entry validity period defaults to seven days unless the authorized workflow sets another period. When a WAITING entry passes its validity period, the system can automatically mark it CANCELLED and lock direct editing. Use the ticket workflow for a correction or review.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why is a record locked?</summary><p>Finalized or expired entries may be locked to protect the record history. If the record requires correction, use <strong>Submit Ticket</strong> where available and include the Control No. and a clear explanation.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should I do before editing a record?</summary><p>Verify the Control No. and beneficiary details first. Make only authorized changes, review the status and office, and confirm the save result before submitting the same action again.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">SWAD OFFICES & FACILITIES</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V8l7-4 7 4v13M9 21v-6h6v6"/></g></svg>Office Selection & Data Scope</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details><summary>How do SWAD office assignments work?</summary><p>SWAD users are associated with their assigned office. Office assignment controls the relevant work queue and access scope. Select only the office that matches the actual assistance entry.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the difference between the Region II and province chat groups?</summary><p>The Region II group is for broad coordination. Province and office groups are intended for their respective members. Group availability and message access are controlled by the server and the current user's role and office.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does switching offices move or duplicate records?</summary><p>No. Changing the active workspace or office context does not itself transfer, duplicate, or merge records. Use the record's authorized office and follow the ticket or administrative process for corrections.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">REPORTS & FUNDS</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="15" rx="2"/><path d="M8 3v4M16 3v4M4 10h16M8 14h3M8 17h7"/></g></svg>Reporting Period, Editable Sheet & Region II Fund</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details><summary>How do I display a report for a selected period?</summary><p>Choose the year and month in the Reporting Period section, then select <strong>Display Selected Period Report</strong>. Review the period and figures before exporting or printing.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I edit the report sheet?</summary><p>The editable report sheet provides toolbar actions for permitted in-sheet edits, row or column sizing, and exports. These presentation edits do not automatically change the underlying assistance records unless the page explicitly indicates that it is saving to the database.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I export the report?</summary><p>Use the sheet toolbar's Excel-compatible export or the print option and select Save as PDF in the browser print dialog. Check the print preview and page orientation before saving.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why does the fund balance differ from the released amount?</summary><p>The Region II fund summary reflects the fund ledger and released assistance totals used by AICS. Check the selected period, status, fund downloads, and report date range before comparing totals. Do not manually adjust financial values to force a match.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do report-sheet edits change the masterlist?</summary><p>No, not by default. The report worksheet is intended for report preparation. Treat official masterlist records and the fund ledger as the source of record.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">CHAT & NOTIFICATIONS</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 11.5a7.5 7.5 0 0 1-8 7.5 8.7 8.7 0 0 1-4.2-1.1L4 19l1.2-3.1A7.2 7.2 0 0 1 4.5 12 7.5 7.5 0 0 1 12 4.5a7.5 7.5 0 0 1 8 7z"/><path d="M8.5 12h.01M12 12h.01M15.5 12h.01"/></g></svg>Communication & Issue Reporting</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details><summary>How do I use Chat?</summary><p>Open Chat, select a direct conversation or a group available to your account, enter your message, and send it. Use the Control No. or page name when reporting a system issue, but include only the minimum information needed.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I edit or delete a message?</summary><p>Use the message actions shown for messages you are authorized to manage. Administrative clearing is restricted to authorized administrators. Message history and read state are maintained separately from MAIFIP's chat data.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why is a chat group or user missing?</summary><p>Group and directory visibility depend on active accounts, office membership, and permissions. If the missing conversation should be available, submit a ticket with the group name and your assigned office.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should I do if the notification bell does not open?</summary><p>Wait for the panel to finish loading, then refresh once if it remains unavailable. If the problem persists, report the page, approximate time, and visible error through the ticket workflow.</p></details>
<details><summary>What information should a good support ticket include?</summary><p>Use this structure: <strong>Page → Control No. or group → Action performed → Expected result → Actual result/error</strong>. Do not attach passwords, reset codes, database credentials, or unnecessary personal information.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">SHEET TOOLS & DATA SAFETY</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3 20 6v5c0 5-3.4 8.5-8 10-4.6-1.5-8-5-8-10V6z"/><path d="m8.5 12 2.2 2.2 4.8-5"/></g></svg>Exporting, Imports & Safe Work Practices</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details><summary>What is the difference between masterlist search and the editable sheet?</summary><p>Search and filters help locate records in the normal masterlist. The editable sheet presents a spreadsheet-style view and exposes only the actions allowed for that workspace and user role.</p></details>
<details><summary>How should I handle an exported file?</summary><p>Save exports in an approved location, share them only with authorized recipients, and remove unnecessary copies when no longer needed. Exported spreadsheets may contain sensitive assistance information.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should I do if an export or save fails?</summary><p>Check whether the browser blocked the download, verify that your session is still active, and try once more. If the problem continues, note the page and error and submit a ticket. Avoid repeated submissions when the first result is uncertain.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should I never send through Chat or a ticket?</summary><p>Never send passwords, one-time codes, database credentials, or other authentication secrets. Include only the minimum record details needed for the authorized support task.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">TROUBLESHOOTING</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M3 9h18M7 6.5h.01M10 6.5h.01M12 13v3M12 11h.01"/></g></svg>Browser, Navigation & Common Errors</h3></div></div><div class="help-faq-grid">
<details><summary>Why did I return to the dashboard or system selection page?</summary><p>Your session or workspace selection may have expired or become inconsistent. Sign in again, select the correct workspace, and reopen the page. If it happens repeatedly, report the page and steps that triggered it.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why does the page look different after an update?</summary><p>The browser may have cached older CSS or JavaScript. Reload the page once or reopen the workspace. If the layout is still broken, include your browser, page name, and a screenshot in the support ticket.</p></details>
<details><summary>What should I do if a page is slow?</summary><p>Wait for the current action to finish before clicking again. Check your connection, refresh once if necessary, and note whether the delay affects one page or the entire workspace.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I contact support?</summary><p>Use the <strong>Open Ticket</strong> button to report system issues, account concerns, or record corrections. Include the Control No. when applicable and never include authentication secrets.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="help-section panel"><div class="panel-heading compact"><div><span class="section-kicker">CONTACT & SUPPORT</span><h3><svg class="help-heading-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M9.5 9a2.7 2.7 0 1 1 4.7 1.8c-1.4 1.2-2.2 1.6-2.2 3.2M12 17h.01"/></g></svg>Need Assistance?</h3></div></div><div class="help-quick-tips"><p>For system-specific issues, open a ticket from the application. For general LPGMA office inquiries, use the contact information published on the official LPGMA website.</p><a class="primary-btn" href="tickets.php">Open Support Ticket</a> <a class="secondary-btn" href="https://lpgma.com.ph/contact-us/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official LPGMA Contact Page</a></div></section>
